WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.735
-My first guest
is a six-time Emmy winner

00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:04.837
and one half
of the co-hosting team

00:00:04.837 --> 00:00:07.774
of the #1 syndicated
daytime talk show,

00:00:07.774 --> 00:00:09.909
"Live with Kelly and Ryan."

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:13.212
She also produces
the true crime series "Exhumed,"

00:00:13.212 --> 00:00:16.983
which returns with back-to-back
episodes February 14th

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:18.451
at 7:00 p.m. on Oxygen.

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:21.554
Here is the one and only
Kelly Ripa.

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:23.189
-Oh, my goodness.
-Thank you.

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:24.691
-Kelly --
-That is so nice.

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:25.925
-That's a good intro
right there.

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:27.960
Welcome back to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:29.562
You know we love
having you here.

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:31.631
It's always good to see you.

00:00:31.631 --> 00:00:32.999
-I love being with you,

00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:38.204
even if it's from this strange
setup in my bedroom.

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:39.972
-Oh.
-I feel like I --

00:00:39.972 --> 00:00:43.509
I mean, I feel like
this is as close as infidelity

00:00:43.509 --> 00:00:46.112
as I will ever get.
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:48.214
Dude, it feels like
we're FaceTiming each other.

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:50.550
Like, this is, like,
"Hey, what's up?"

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.284
yeah, which we never do,
but why not?

00:00:52.284 --> 00:00:54.853
We can be besties
and be best friends.

00:00:54.853 --> 00:00:57.223
Like, what's happening?
Tell me all the goss.

00:00:57.223 --> 00:00:59.292
How is the family doing,

00:00:59.292 --> 00:01:03.295
and how is 2021 going so far?

00:01:03.295 --> 00:01:06.365
-You know, I don't know
what I thought.

00:01:06.365 --> 00:01:11.504
I think I thought, like, 2021
would be like the sequence

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:14.707
of "The Wizard of Oz" where --

00:01:14.707 --> 00:01:17.076
You know when they're
in black and white,

00:01:17.076 --> 00:01:21.413
and then the house lands,
and she opens the door,

00:01:21.413 --> 00:01:24.150
and everything's in color?

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:27.319
I think I thought,
like, 2021 would happen,

00:01:27.319 --> 00:01:30.289
and then, like, it's over.

00:01:30.289 --> 00:01:33.359
We can all come outside, guys,
and go play in the park.

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:35.728
-Yeah.
-Pretty much the same.

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:37.563
-It didn't quite
happen yet, yeah.

00:01:37.563 --> 00:01:40.533
I want to talk to you
about the true crime series

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:42.267
that you produce
called "Exhumed."

00:01:42.267 --> 00:01:44.203
I love the true crime,

00:01:44.203 --> 00:01:45.905
but I have to watch
during the daytime.

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:48.207
I can't do it at nighttime,
or else --

00:01:48.207 --> 00:01:49.642
-What you have to do --

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:53.979
I'm going to plug my show and
do you a favor at the same time.

00:01:53.979 --> 00:01:58.584
So, on Sundays, okay,
on Oxygen Channel,

00:01:58.584 --> 00:02:00.619
they have a "Snapped" marathon.

00:02:00.619 --> 00:02:01.987
Now, do you know
about "Snapped"?

00:02:01.987 --> 00:02:04.256
-Yes, I've seen "Snapped."

00:02:04.256 --> 00:02:07.527
-"Snapped" is basically
hours and hours and hours

00:02:07.527 --> 00:02:11.396
of programming
about women who snap one day

00:02:11.396 --> 00:02:13.165
and kill their spouse.

00:02:13.165 --> 00:02:14.600
-Yep. No, I've seen enough

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:17.937
where I go, "Honey,
it's banned in our house."

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:21.474
-Exactly. And so it started
getting banned in our house.

00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:24.410
Like, I'd be cooking
Sunday dinner,

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:26.112
and you have to understand,

00:02:26.112 --> 00:02:28.348
like, I don't
take pleasure in it.

00:02:28.348 --> 00:02:30.683
I actually do it
with a resentful heart.

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:32.752
So I'd be sitting there,
like, you know,

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:35.054
chopping carrots with an ax,

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:37.323
and the kids are like, "Mom's
watching 'Snapped' again."

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:38.757
-Yeah. Of course.

00:02:38.757 --> 00:02:42.128
-And so that's how we came up
with this idea for a show,

00:02:42.128 --> 00:02:45.531
"Exhumed, which is basically

00:02:45.531 --> 00:02:50.136
what happens when people --

00:02:50.136 --> 00:02:53.806
They die under mysterious
circumstances sometimes,

00:02:53.806 --> 00:02:58.745
and they're buried, and then
suddenly there's a wrinkle,

00:02:58.745 --> 00:03:01.580
and it turns out
maybe this person

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:05.451
had more than one person
in their life that died, right?

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:07.520
And so you have to
exhume the body.

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:11.757
And what better way to celebrate
Valentine's Day, I thought,

00:03:11.757 --> 00:03:14.626
than to have new episodes

00:03:14.626 --> 00:03:16.195
of "Exhumed."
-February 14th,

00:03:16.195 --> 00:03:18.898
there's back-to-back episodes
of "Exhumed."

00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:21.100
I love these shows.
I want to show a clip

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.434
from the new season
of "Exhumed."

00:03:22.434 --> 00:03:24.603
Take a look at this clip.

00:03:24.603 --> 00:03:26.605
-With 46 years
of new developments

00:03:26.605 --> 00:03:28.174
in forensic science,

00:03:28.174 --> 00:03:30.242
the evidence buried with Loretta

00:03:30.242 --> 00:03:33.813
could be the key
to catching Egley.

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:35.448 line:0%
-I call Heidi Jones up,

00:03:35.448 --> 00:03:38.284 line:0%
and I told her we were going
to exhume the body,

00:03:38.284 --> 00:03:41.587 line:0%
and I got exactly
the answer I expected.

00:03:41.587 --> 00:03:45.258 line:0%
-I said, "Get me a shovel.
I'll help dig."

00:03:45.258 --> 00:03:47.059
-Ooh.

00:03:47.059 --> 00:03:50.029
Kelly, I want to congratulate
you, because this is very big.

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:52.998
This month marks
your 20th anniversary

00:03:52.998 --> 00:03:55.201
of co-hosting your show "Live."

00:03:55.201 --> 00:03:58.137
That is an awesome
achievement in television.

00:03:58.137 --> 00:04:00.206
-I keep thinking
that it's three years.

00:04:00.206 --> 00:04:01.874
I'm like,
"It's only been three years.

00:04:01.874 --> 00:04:04.243
I don't understand
what the big deal is."

00:04:04.243 --> 00:04:06.412
-I mean, can you --
What do you remember

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:08.113
about getting the job
in the first place?

00:04:08.113 --> 00:04:10.449
Was this something
that you always imagined?

00:04:10.449 --> 00:04:11.851
-No. Oh, no, no, no.

00:04:11.851 --> 00:04:13.886
I actually think that the fact

00:04:13.886 --> 00:04:19.458
that I did not
have any anticipation

00:04:19.458 --> 00:04:21.127
about getting that job at all

00:04:21.127 --> 00:04:23.463
actually worked greatly
to my advantage,

00:04:23.463 --> 00:04:25.598
because I wasn't going after it.

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:30.536
I was asked to fill in for a
fill-in host at the last minute,

00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:33.373
so it took any stakes
or any, like, nervousness

00:04:33.373 --> 00:04:37.143
that I probably
would have had away.

00:04:37.143 --> 00:04:42.048
My only concern was that
I was very early pregnant

00:04:42.048 --> 00:04:44.050
with our daughter, Lola.
-Yes.

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:47.620
-And nobody knew. Nobody knew.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:50.722
Mark and I knew,
and nobody else knew.

00:04:50.722 --> 00:04:53.326
And they said,
"There's going to be a psychic,

00:04:53.326 --> 00:04:55.260
and she's going
to give you a reading,

00:04:55.260 --> 00:04:57.997
if you don't mind, because
we're doing psychic week."

00:04:57.997 --> 00:05:01.200
And I said to Mark, "I've got to
cancel. I can't do this."

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:02.968
-"She's gonna bust me."

00:05:02.968 --> 00:05:05.604
-Right. And he goes, "Oh, what,

00:05:05.604 --> 00:05:07.807
you think a psychic's going
to figure out you're pregnant?"

00:05:07.807 --> 00:05:10.443
I go, "Well, what if she does?

00:05:10.443 --> 00:05:13.246
Isn't that what,
like, psychics do?"

00:05:13.246 --> 00:05:15.581
And, Jimmy,

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:20.319
not only did she figure out
I was pregnant in three seconds,

00:05:20.319 --> 00:05:23.523
but she was like, "Your
grandmother, Dee, is here."

00:05:23.523 --> 00:05:26.058
And I was like, "Mm, nope,
that's not her name."

00:05:26.058 --> 00:05:28.427
She's like, "Esther,
but her nickname is Dee."

00:05:28.427 --> 00:05:31.831
Like, she figured it all out.

00:05:31.831 --> 00:05:33.366
-No, I don't know
if I could handle it.

00:05:33.366 --> 00:05:35.401
That's wild stuff.

00:05:35.401 --> 00:05:38.738
Hey, over the incredible
20 years that you've hosted,

00:05:38.738 --> 00:05:40.005
there have been so many
memorable moments,

00:05:40.005 --> 00:05:41.307
and I wanted to challenge you

00:05:41.307 --> 00:05:43.742
just to see how many
of those moments you remember

00:05:43.742 --> 00:05:46.011
in the
"Know Your Show Challenge."

00:05:46.011 --> 00:05:48.347
Alright, I'm gonna ask a series
of rapid-fire questions,

00:05:48.347 --> 00:05:49.982
You have to answer
as fast as possible

00:05:49.982 --> 00:05:51.283
or whatever you want to do.

00:05:51.283 --> 00:05:54.119
You're Kelly Ripa.
Please. Alright.

00:05:54.119 --> 00:05:57.289
Who was your first celebrity
guest interview as co-host?

00:05:57.289 --> 00:06:00.626
-I know that. Ray Liotta.

00:06:00.626 --> 00:06:02.361
-Number 2, who was
your celebrity guest

00:06:02.361 --> 00:06:06.332
on your show this morning?

00:06:06.332 --> 00:06:08.667
-Uh...
[ Both laugh ]

00:06:08.667 --> 00:06:10.169
-That's the best part.

00:06:10.169 --> 00:06:12.371
[ Both laugh ]

00:06:12.371 --> 00:06:14.607
That is the best part.
I've done it, too.

00:06:14.607 --> 00:06:16.342
I've done it, too.
-If I asked you --

00:06:16.342 --> 00:06:18.845
At 1:00 a.m., if I asked you,

00:06:18.845 --> 00:06:20.779
you would not know that
I was here.

00:06:20.779 --> 00:06:23.081
-[ Chuckles ]
You, of course, I would know.

00:06:23.081 --> 00:06:24.316
Alright. Good. I got you.

00:06:24.316 --> 00:06:26.219
You broke
a Guinness World Record

00:06:26.219 --> 00:06:29.755
for getting something thrown at
your face 24 times in a minute.

00:06:29.755 --> 00:06:31.824
What was it?

00:06:31.824 --> 00:06:34.226
-I think pies.

00:06:34.226 --> 00:06:36.662
-Yes, it was banana cream pies.

00:06:36.662 --> 00:06:37.896
-Okay, amazing.

00:06:37.896 --> 00:06:39.298
-You've done everything.

00:06:39.298 --> 00:06:43.635
How many Daytime Emmy Awards
have you won for "Live"?

00:06:43.635 --> 00:06:45.304
-Oh, for -- I don't know.

00:06:45.304 --> 00:06:47.840
I heard you say that I won six,

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:50.008
which I think is also incorrect,

00:06:50.008 --> 00:06:52.278
but I'm going to say like three.
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:52.278 --> 00:06:53.479
-Three?
-It's COVID.

00:06:53.479 --> 00:06:55.548
We have no research department.
Give us a break.

00:06:55.548 --> 00:06:58.617
-I don't know.
-Three. You won more than three.

00:06:58.617 --> 00:06:59.751
-I don't know.

00:06:59.751 --> 00:07:02.255
-Oh, this question
is really from the heart.

00:07:02.255 --> 00:07:06.758
You have very high stools
on your show.

00:07:06.758 --> 00:07:11.464
My question is, have you ever
fallen off your stool while
taping?

00:07:11.464 --> 00:07:14.433
-I've -- Oh.

00:07:14.433 --> 00:07:17.102
I don't think so.
I would say no.

00:07:17.102 --> 00:07:19.771
-Has your co-host
ever fallen off the stool?

00:07:19.771 --> 00:07:22.074
-Yes. Yes.
[ Both laugh ]

00:07:22.074 --> 00:07:24.276
We have a hard time
keeping him in the stool.

00:07:24.276 --> 00:07:25.544
-I want to show a clip,

00:07:25.544 --> 00:07:28.213
'cause we've only shown it
50 times on our show.

00:07:28.213 --> 00:07:29.748
Please roll the tape.
-Us, too.

00:07:29.748 --> 00:07:30.849
-It's my favorite thing.

00:07:30.849 --> 00:07:33.019
-Gold from Buffalo, New York.

00:07:33.019 --> 00:07:36.822
Lookit. [ Laughs ]

00:07:36.822 --> 00:07:39.559
It's the best thing ever. Ah.
Thanks for --

00:07:39.559 --> 00:07:41.260
Let's keep more
of those memories going.

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:42.594
Here's to 20 more.

00:07:42.594 --> 00:07:44.764
Congratulations on your
20th anniversary of "Live."

00:07:44.764 --> 00:07:47.667
And be sure, everybody,
check out "Exhumed" on Oxygen

00:07:47.667 --> 00:07:50.002
on Valentine's Day.
It's a back-to-back episode.

00:07:50.002 --> 00:07:51.237
Kelly Ripa, we love you.

